\f1\fs22 By three songs in, the High Elvis had the audience eating out of his deep fryer. He\'92d already delivered most of his trademark moves, which the Elvi in the audience mimicked flawlessly, the Cloudborne copied earnestly, while the Airborne exaggerated every move with a lack of finesse that declared, 
\f2\i Who cares? We\'92ve got trust funds
\f1\i0 . The older members of the crowd practiced cowboy struts, smouldering stares and wiggled fingers at complete strangers. The younger swivelled hips and went rubber legs. Some mimicked windmills and others attempted karate kicks\'97with and without air guitars.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 The crowd sensed the show was almost over when the lighting dimmed and caressed the High Elvis centre-stage. He took a mic from a stand and went to the stage\'92s edge, between fold-backs. There he stood quiet and waited for the audience to match his mood, the began speaking like a man talking over a fence at dusk to a neighbour he happened to like. \
\'93We are the lucky ones, most never join the race.\'94 the High Elvis looked up at the Colonel and chuckled at its tether. \'93The Dawkins said that.\'94\

\f2\i High Elvis! Praise the Dawkins! 
\f1\i0 came the cheer from Elvi down the front.\
\'93Whether Elvi, or Cloudborne, or Airborne, evolution produced us all, just the same.\'94\
For a moment the lawn did nothing at all. Then somebody a long way back 
\f2\i whooped
\f1\i0 .\

\f2\i Evolution! Whoo!
\f1\i0 \
\'93I want to thank all the bands who came, who played, and who never once left the building. I want to thank the Three Sages of the Travelator for their public service announcement, and for a ukulele solo that will probably live forever in defiance of everything the Dawkins ever taught us about the survival of the fittest.\'94
\f2\i\fs24 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \

\fs22 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Dawkins! Dawkins! Fittest! Fittest!\

\f1\i0 \'93Thank you, very much. You have been a beautiful audience, and I mean that in the strictest scientific sense. Out of everything that could have crawled up out of the one long blind accident, it was you lot who made it here tonight.
\f2\i\fs24 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \

\f1\i0\fs22 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\'93I want to thank our Airborne friends, who went twelve rounds with their first Elvi cocktails today\'85 and argued with the trees about for hours after.\'94\
\'93Now, before the last song, I am going to ask something of you\'97when you go home tonight, you will take your rubbish with you. Every wrapper. Every unglued sideburn. We cleaned up the Ghetto, brothers and sisters. We shovelled, we scrubbed, we hosed. We did not do all that so we could ride up here and leave somebody else\'92s lawn looking like the good old days. When we walk off this grass, the only proof we were ever here will be the songs and the memories\'85\'94\

\f2\i Clean the Domain! Clean the Domain!
\f1\i0 \
He let it hang. \'93Well.\'94 he clutched the mic. \'93The Great Teacher has a few thoughts\'85\'94\
The crowd roared. There hadn\'92t been a new song on the streams in months.\
\'93
\f2\i Viva la evoluci\'f3n!
\f1\i0  This is Religious Minds!\'94\
The band launched and it was like they\'92d flicked the switch on a substation that electrified the whole audience. The light show found a few thousand more watts among the LED batten cases. It was said later that the ground shook and almost burst the Bubbles.\
The first lines were peak High Elvis, delivered with as much warmth and charisma as power.\
